tool_use_result.stdout:
  "decision": "v1.1 adds exactly five web-only components — Avatar, Breadcrumb, Divider, Timeline, DescriptionList — one at a time, each behind a Figma approval gate and a final approval gate. Native parity is logged in candidates.json, not built. Semantic tokens these five need have standing approval and go Figma foundations first, then packages/tokens, then the component.",
  "date": "2026-09-24"
},
{
  "id": "DEC-010",
  "topic": "Avatar design",
  "decision": "Avatar follows the ReUI reference (Type Image|Text|Icon × Size × boolean Show status / Show badge icon, status as an instance swap defaulting to success) plus a Shape property circle|squircle. Sizes xs|sm|md|lg|xl = spacing/5|6|8|10|12; the 10px status dot maps to spacing/2. Squircle is a rounded square via avatar-squircle-radius-{size} tokens aliasing existing radii (no Figma-only smoothing). AvatarGroup overlap is the avatar-group-overlap token (-spacing/2). No disabled state; Avatar is presentational. Image alt: informative → meaningful alt, decorative beside a name → alt=\"\", failed image → initials → icon.",
  "date": "2026-09-25"
},
{
  "id": "DEC-011",
  "topic": "Breadcrumb design",
  "decision": "Breadcrumb follows the ReUI reference: a Breadcrumb set (Separator chevron|dot) plus a BreadcrumbItem set (Type Link|Current Page|Dropdown|Ellipsis × State Default|Hover|Focus), one family. Links are a plain <a> in brand primary (foreground on hover); Current Page uses foreground; Dropdown and separators use foreground-muted. Ellipsis button is spacing/6 with radius/md. The Dropdown item is a trigger only (aria-haspopup=menu); its menu is supplied by the caller. Focus uses the Atlas focus-ring at border-width/2. No new tokens.",
  "date": "2026-09-25"
},
{
  "id": "DEC-012",
  "topic": "DropdownMenu added to v1.1",
  "decision": "DropdownMenu (ReUI node 42817:7410) is added as a sixth v1.1 web component, its own phase after Breadcrumb, with its own Figma and final approval gates. Adding @radix-ui/react-dropdown-menu is NOT yet approved; decide when the phase reaches code. Supersedes the 'exactly five' wording of DEC-009.",
  "date": "2026-09-25"
},
{
  "id": "DEC-013",
  "topic": "Divider design",
  "decision": "Divider follows the ReUI Separator page (node 42834:6882): a flat 1px line, Orientation horizontal|vertical × Tone default|strong|subtle|inverse (border, border-strong, border-subtle, border-inverse). Divider and Separator are one component. New semantic token border-inverse aliases color/neutral/0 in Light and Dark (opaque, like foreground-on-brand; Figma variables cannot alias with alpha). Labelled and inset dividers are out of v1.1 (the reference draws neither). Meaningful divider = role=separator (hr for horizontal, aria-orientation=vertical for vertical); decorative = role=none. No states, no motion.",
  "date": "2026-09-25"
},
{
  "id": "DEC-014",
  "topic": "ListItem replaces DescriptionList",
  "decision": "The fifth v1.1 component is ListItem (compositions), not DescriptionList: the ReUI Item (node 42824:12448) is a media-object row, not a key-value list. Figma: List Item (Direction horizontal|vertical × Variant default|outline|muted × Size sm|md) plus List Item Media (Type icon|tile|image × Size). Sizes follow Atlas sm|md (shadcn xs → sm; default and sm are identical → md). The shadcn 10px values snap to spacing/3 and radius/lg (12px); the image radius is radius/sm (4px). Media, title, description and actions are individually hideable; Actions holds a Button (Button sm, 32px) or an icon. Vertical media fills the width at 3:2. No new tokens; no contract (contracts stay Avatar and Divider only). Text line-height is 150% (title, md description) and 135% (sm description) in Figma, matching line-height-normal and line-height-snug.",
  "date": "2026-09-25"
},
{
  "id": "DEC-015",
  "topic": "Code tokens added to Figma foundations",
  "decision": "Figma follows code where code already had a token Figma lacked: Atlas/Primitives gained spacing/9 (36), radius/base (8, radius/md now aliases it), font-weight/*, font-family/*, line-height/* (ratios), letter-spacing/* (em), duration/*, easing/*, each with WEB code syntax; and effect styles shadow/sm|md|lg|xl (light values — dark shadow values stay code-only, since effect styles have no modes). line-height, letter-spacing, duration and easing are hidden from pickers (scopes []) because Figma cannot bind them. Figma has layout/container/* (640–1536) that code does not define; it is unused and left as is.",
  "date": "2026-09-25"
},
{
  "id": "DEC-016",
  "topic": "DropdownMenu design and no external dependency",
  "decision": "DropdownMenu follows the shadcn Community reference (node 114:21467, file LhQn47HBQtxfXbIvDdIgzV), replacing ReUI node 42817:7410 in DEC-012. Atlas is its own library, so no external dependency is added: @radix-ui/react-dropdown-menu is NOT installed and DEC-012's pending approval is closed. The menu is built with React and react-dom (portal, anchored placement, roving focus, typeahead, submenus). Tier patterns. Figma: Dropdown Menu Item (Type item|destructive|checkbox|radio × State default|focus|disabled), Dropdown Menu Label, Dropdown Menu (Groups 1–3, Show Label). Item radius is radius-sm (4px; the reference is 6px, which Atlas lacks). Row line-height 150% makes a row 33px. Disabled opacity is 0.5 set directly because Figma opacity variables are percentages. BreadcrumbDropdown is wired to the menu through DropdownMenuTrigger asChild, superseding the trigger-only rule in DEC-011. Sides are bottom|top as drawn; no collision flip, no motion. Contracts stay Avatar and Divider only.",
  "date": "2026-09-25"
},
{
  "id": "DEC-017",
  "topic": "background-accent token added",
  "decision": "New semantic token background-accent (Light color/neutral/100, Dark color/neutral/700), added to Figma foundations first, then to the code tokens. It is the highlighted-row fill for menus and lists. It exists because background-muted and surface-overlay are both neutral/800 in Dark, which hid the focused row in the DropdownMenu. Bound to the focus state of Dropdown Menu Item (item, checkbox, radio); destructive focus keeps danger-subtle. Closes CAND-012.",
  "date": "2026-09-25"
},
{
  "id": "DEC-018",
  "topic": "Spinner variants, sizes, motion and icon-stroke tokens",
  "decision": "Spinner (primitives) follows ReUI Spinner node 42836:15305 (file BOJ49F6rceAmcCC70lSiav): Variant default (Lucide loader-circle) | custom (Lucide loader). Figma values are lowercase like every other Atlas set (the reference's Default/Custom were renamed at the user's request). Sizes xs 16 | sm 20 | md 24 | lg 32 are added beyond the reference (one 16px size) at the user's request, mapped to icon-size tokens. Glyphs are inline SVG paths, no icon dependency. Tokens added Figma first: duration/spin 1000ms (Atlas/Primitives) with easing-linear; code gets --atlas-duration-spin and the existing Figma icon/stroke/* as --atlas-icon-stroke-* (1.5 | 1.75 | 2 | 2.25). Nested icon strokes cannot bind variables in Figma, so stroke weights there are set to those values. Rotation stops under prefers-reduced-motion. role=status with a visually hidden label, default Loading. Standalone: Button is not changed (CAND-014).",
  "date": "2026-09-26"
},
{
  "id": "DEC-019",
  "topic": "Skeleton as a single primitive with pulse tokens",
  "decision": "Skeleton (primitives) follows ReUI node 42836:14236 but is one block with Shape rect | circle, not the reference's five Avatar/Card/Text/Form/Table variants; those are composed examples on the Figma page. Fill background-muted, radius radius/md (rect) and radius/full (circle), default 16 tall (spacing/4) and 40 for circle (spacing/10), no size property. Motion is a pulse: opacity 1 to opacity/pulse and back over duration/pulse with easing/standard, stopped under prefers-reduced-motion. New tokens verified missing in Atlas (durations were 0/120/200/320/1000 and opacities .5/.9/.6, with disabled semantically wrong), added Figma first then code: duration/pulse 2000ms, opacity/pulse 0.5. The block is aria-hidden with no role; the loading container sets aria-busy and owns any announcement. Image will reuse Skeleton for its loading state.",
  "date": "2026-09-26"
},
{
  "id": "DEC-020",
  "topic": "Image as a plain img wrapper reusing Skeleton",
  "decision": "Image (primitives) follows ReUI node 42732:27744 (Aspect Ratio, nine fixed-width variants) as one primitive: Figma properties Ratio (1:1, 4:3, 3:2, 16:9, 16:10, 9:16, 3:4, 2:3, 4:5, auto) and State (loaded, loading, error), 12 variants (ten loaded ratios plus loading and error at 1:1). Fit (cover default, contain) and radius (none, sm, md default, lg, xl, full; radius tokens) are code props, not Figma variants; a fallback slot replaces the default error block (background-muted, Lucide image-off at icon/size/lg, foreground-subtle). Loading renders a Skeleton until onLoad and a cached image skips it. auto keeps natural size (Figma draws it 300x200; loading and error under auto use 3:2). alt is required in the type; an empty alt makes the default fallback aria-hidden. Plain img, not next/image. No new tokens: radius, background-muted, foreground-subtle, icon-size-lg, icon-stroke-lg and the Skeleton pulse tokens all exist. Figma loaded variants use a token-bound stand-in scene (info-muted, warning, success) because a page cannot embed a photo; the icon stroke weight is numeric because nested icon strokes cannot bind icon/stroke/lg.",
  "date": "2026-09-26"
},
{
  "id": "DEC-021",
  "topic": "Progress as a plain role=progressbar primitive",
  "decision": "Progress (primitives) follows ReUI node 42829:9378 as one 4px bar, not the reference's 11 Progress= variants and not its thumb (Slider owns that). Figma property State (determinate, indeterminate), 2 variants; value and max are props (DEC-003), the Figma fill is drawn at 50%. Track background-muted, fill primary (not the reference's black), height spacing/1, radius radius/full; no new tokens. Fill width animates with duration/base and easing/standard. Indeterminate slides a 40% segment over duration/pulse (2000ms) with easing/linear, reusing the existing tokens (user accepted the recommendation); both motions stop under prefers-reduced-motion, and the static indeterminate segment sits at 30%. Plain div role=progressbar, no Radix: aria-valuemin 0, aria-valuemax, aria-valuenow (omitted when indeterminate), name from label, aria-label or aria-labelledby, helper text via aria-describedby, and an optional aria-valuetext prop (user accepted). Follow-up (user, 2026-09-26): like the reference, Figma has a Progress wrapper set (541:28: State plus Label, Value and Helper switches and text, a label row, the bar and helper text) around an internal .Progress / Bar set (538:7, scaled fill); Code Connect and the sync point at the wrapper. The thumb is not drawn (Slider owns it). The Figma Examples use the bar with loose text and overlay fills for the non-50% widths because the Plugin API cannot resize a fill inside an instance.",
  "date": "2026-09-26"
},
{
  "id": "DEC-022",
  "topic": "RadioGroup as a native-input compound primitive",
  "decision": "RadioGroup (primitives) is a compound export RadioGroup + RadioGroupItem in one folder, built on native input type=radio with appearance none (no Radix, Q3/Q9). Figma has two sets mirroring the reference Radio / Group and Radio / Button: Radio Group (545:98: Direction vertical | horizontal x Variant default | card) and Radio Group Item (544:283: Variant default | card x Checked unchecked | checked x Size sm | md x State default | hover | focus-visible | disabled | invalid, plus Label and Description switches and text); Code Connect and the sync point at the group, the sync lists both sets' properties on it. Group Variant is an addition to the reference so the card group can be drawn. Sizes sm 16 and md 20 (as Checkbox), dot 8 (spacing/2) at both. Checked = primary fill with a primary-foreground dot (danger fill and danger-foreground dot when invalid); unchecked = background fill, border-strong ring; hover = background-subtle fill and foreground ring (no separate pressed state); invalid = danger ring, no red label; disabled = opacity/disabled 0.5, set by hand in Figma because a node opacity cannot bind to a 0 to 1 variable. Card = radius/md, padding 12 by 16, checked = primary border and primary-subtle fill (dark mode blends primary into surface-raised, as Checkbox card). Focus ring 2 focus-ring with a 2 offset on the radio only (a separate ring layer in Figma). The reference's second, right-side radio is not built (indicator at the start). Selection state lives on the group (value, defaultValue, onValueChange); the item's Checked axis is not a prop. No new tokens. CAND-011 closed by this component; DropdownMenuRadioItem keeps its own 8 dot because a menu item is not a native radio.",
  "date": "2026-09-26"
},
{
  "id": "DEC-023",
  "topic": "Slider as a custom pointer-event primitive with range and vertical",
  "decision": "Slider (primitives) is a custom pointer-event implementation, no Radix and no native range input (user, 2026-09-26): it supports a range (two thumbs that cannot cross) and a vertical orientation in v1, unlike the reference which draws horizontal single and range only. Figma has three sets mirroring the reference Slider, .Slider / Bar and .Slider / Toggle: Slider (550:241: Orientation horizontal | vertical x Range false | true x State default | disabled, plus Label, Value, Helper, Leading and Trailing switches and text), .Slider / Bar (550:96: Orientation x Range x Disabled) and .Slider / Toggle (550:15: the thumb, State default | hover | focus-visible); Code Connect and the sync point at the Slider set. The reference's 11 Progress= variants are not built (value, min, max and step are props, DEC-003); the Figma bar is drawn at 50 and at 30 to 70, and its Helper is one text, not two labels. Track spacing/1 background-muted radius/full, fill primary (as Progress). Thumb 16 (spacing/4) with a 2 primary border, surface fill and shadow/sm, not the reference's 12 grey-ring thumb (user accepted); hover and dragging add a 4 primary-subtle halo, focus-visible a 2 focus-ring ring with a 2 gap on the thumb only; disabled opacity 0.5 (set by hand in Figma). The pointer hit area is 44 (touch/min) via a pseudo-element, visual size unchanged. No new tokens. API: range makes value a [low, high] pair (value, defaultValue, onValueChange), min 0, max 100, step 1, orientation, disabled, name (hidden inputs), label, valueLabel, helperText, leading, trailing and getAriaValueText. Each thumb is role=slider with aria-valuemin, aria-valuemax (a range thumb's bounds are the other thumb), aria-valuenow, aria-valuetext and aria-orientation; arrows step, PageUp and PageDown take 10 steps, Home and End jump to the thumb's bounds; RTL mirrors the horizontal track and its arrow keys, vertical runs bottom to top. Range thumbs are named Minimum and Maximum. No marks, steps drawn on the track, tooltip or value bubble.",
  "date": "2026-09-26"
},
{
  "id": "DEC-024",
  "topic": "Button xs size, Icon only property and icon slots",
  "decision": "Button keeps its touch-friendly scale (sm 32, md 40, lg 48) and adds xs 24 (user, 2026-09-27): height spacing/6, padding-inline spacing/2, gap spacing/1, font-size/xs, radius/md, all existing tokens. Size is xs | sm | md | lg; the legacy Size=icon is retired, and a square icon button is the new Figma variant property Icon only=true at every size (24, 32, 40, 48), matching the iconOnly prop and DEC-003. Figma Button (19:2) now has 288 variants: Variant x Size x Icon only x State. Icon slots are Figma properties: Leading icon and Trailing icon (boolean, default off) with Leading icon slot and Trailing icon slot (instance swap, default Lucide plus), and Icon (instance swap) for icon-only; slots are not drawn in the loading state, which shows the spinner in place of the leading icon. xs icon glyph is 12, other sizes 16. xs and sm expand to touch/min (44) on pointer: coarse, as sm did; xs is otherwise desktop-density. Code: ButtonSize drops icon, callers use iconOnly.",
  "date": "2026-09-27"
},
{
  "id": "DEC-025",
  "topic": "Switch invalid gets a visual: Invalid boolean + danger ring",
  "decision": "Switch (primitives) DISC-028 resolved (user, 2026-09-27): an invalid Switch gets a visual, modelled in Figma as a new BOOLEAN property `Invalid` (default false, DEC-003 — a value-carrying prop is its own property, not folded into State) rather than a 6th State value. Figma Switch (95:114) also had its `Variant` axis renamed to `Checked` (off | on) in the same pass, matching the Checkbox precedent (DISC-004/013). Each of the 30 variants got an `Invalid Ring` overlay frame — stroke-only, 2px, bound to `color/danger`, corner-radius full, 2px outset from the track, `strokeAlign: OUTSIDE` — with its `visible` property bound to the new Invalid boolean via componentPropertyReferences, default hidden. Code: `.track[data-invalid]:not(:focus-visible)` applies a matching `outline: 2px solid var(--atlas-danger)` with `outline-offset: 2px` (existing `--atlas-border-width-2` / `--atlas-spacing-0_5` tokens, no new tokens); the `:not(:focus-visible)` guard keeps the focus ring visually dominant when both are true. `invalid` was already a prop (aria-invalid + data-invalid); no API change, only the missing CSS/Figma pairing.",
  "date": "2026-09-27"
},
{
  "id": "DEC-026",
  "topic": "NavBar variant reconciliation: elevated ≈ floating, 4-way default/bordered/floating/transparent",
  "decision": "NavBar (layouts) DISC-010/025/026 resolved (user, 2026-09-27): code's `elevated` and Figma's `floating` are the same concept (shadow-raised, no border) and are unified by rename rather than kept as two separate values. Inspecting Figma NavBar (148:306) node properties showed the three existing variants are not a straight rename target: Figma `default` (fill `surface`, cornerRadius 4, no border, no shadow) has no prior code equivalent; Figma `bordered` (fill `surface`, cornerRadius 4, 1px `border-subtle` stroke) is what code's old `default` actually drew; Figma `floating` (fill `surface-raised`, cornerRadius 16, 2-layer drop shadow) is what code's `elevated` drew, minus the radius. Final NavBarVariant (both sides): `default | bordered | floating | transparent`. Figma: added a `transparent` variant (no fill/border/shadow, cornerRadius 4, at all 3 sizes × 2 states) to the set — code's `transparent` had no Figma equivalent before. Code: new bare `default` (`--atlas-surface`, `--atlas-radius-sm`, no border/shadow); old `default` renamed to `bordered` (`--atlas-surface`, `--atlas-border-subtle` bottom border, `--atlas-radius-sm`) — also corrected from `--atlas-background`/`--atlas-border` to the `surface`/`border-subtle` tokens Figma actually binds, since `background` and `surface` diverge in dark mode; `elevated` renamed to `floating` (`--atlas-surface-raised`, `--atlas-shadow-lg` — closest existing token to Figma's custom 2-layer shadow, up from the old `shadow-md`, `--atlas-radius-xl` matching Figma's 16px); `transparent` unchanged in behaviour, gains `--atlas-radius-sm` per the user's 'adopt Figma's radius' choice, and its `.scrolled` fallback moves to the same `surface`/`border-subtle` tokens for consistency. No new tokens — `--atlas-radius-sm`/`-xl` and `--atlas-surface`/`-raised` already existed. `NavBarHeader` (mobile-native anatomy, no linked Figma node) only had its `elevated` class renamed to `floating` to keep the shared `NavBarVariant` type working; its visual treatment (tokens, no radius) is unchanged from before this task.",
  "date": "2026-09-27"
},
{
  "id": "DEC-027",
  "topic": "Drawer promoted to a standalone component; Dialog's drawer narrowing sequenced after it",
  "decision": "Drawer (compositions) split out of the old DISC-008 scope per docs/componentlist plan _dashboard-gaps_2026-09-27.md §4 (user, 2026-09-27): Figma had no sheet/drawer content, so this is new-component work (CAND-020, promoted this task), not a gap fix. Sequencing: because NavBar's mobile hamburger menu was a real production consumer of Dialog's `variant=\"drawer\"`, the user chose to build and ship Drawer (and migrate NavBar onto it) BEFORE narrowing DialogVariant to `default | destructive` (the later, separate A3 task) — reordering the plan's default A3-then-A3c order to avoid breaking NavBar on `main`. Figma: new page + component set `Drawer` (577:24), reference shadcn/ReUI Drawer (`BOJ49F6rceAmcCC70lSiav:42812:7238`, screenshotted per the plan's strengthened audit rule) confirmed the anatomy (header with inline close, description, content, footer) and that Atlas's own shipped `.drawer`/`[data-side]` CSS (in Dialog.module.css, previously undocumented in Figma) already matched the reference's edge-anchored, hinge-corner-rounded, shadowed card — so geometry was lifted from that shipped code rather than re-derived from the reference's pixels. Figma property: `Side` = `start | end` only (2 variants) — no `top`/`bottom` (no consumer), no `Size` (kept code-only, reusing Dialog's existing `--atlas-dialog-sm/md/lg/xl/full` tokens, no new tokens), no `State=loading` (no consumer). Code: `compositions/Drawer/Drawer.tsx` re-exports `Dialog as Drawer`, `DialogTrigger`, `DialogHeader`, `DialogTitle`, `DialogDescription`, `DialogBody`, `DialogFooter`, `DialogClose` directly from Dialog (same Radix a11y wiring, zero duplication); only `DrawerContent` is new, with its own `Drawer.module.css` lifting Dialog's overlay/content-base/drawer rules verbatim. No drag handle (Sheet-only, per BUG-037/066 precedent). NavBar.tsx migrated its mobile menu from `<DialogContent variant=\"drawer\" side=\"start\">` to `<DrawerContent side=\"start\">`; the app/page.tsx sandbox's drawer demo migrated the same way. Dialog.tsx's `DialogVariant` union and its own `.drawer`/`.sheet` CSS are untouched by this task — that removal is the separate, later A3 task, done only once nothing depends on Dialog's drawer presentation.",
  "date": "2026-09-27"
},
{
  "id": "DEC-028",
  "topic": "Sheet promoted to a standalone component, 4-way Side; Dialog's sheet narrowing remains the later A3 task",
  "decision": "Sheet (compositions) split out of the old DISC-008 scope per docs/componentlist plan _dashboard-gaps_2026-09-27.md §4 (user, 2026-09-27), same sequencing logic DEC-027 used for Drawer: Dialog's `variant=\"sheet\"` was still the live consumer in the app/page.tsx sandbox, so Sheet ships standalone (CAND-021, promoted this task) before Dialog's own `DialogVariant`/`.sheet` CSS narrowing (A3, still separate and later). Reference checked: ReUI Sheet (`BOJ49F6rceAmcCC70lSiav:42834:6947`, screenshotted per the plan's strengthened audit rule) draws a 4-side (bottom/top/left/right), flat-corner, no-shadow card. User chose to diverge from the reference on two points, confirmed before any Figma write: (1) 4-way `Side = bottom | top | start | end` (not bottom-only, even though start/end duplicate Drawer's own geometry) and (2) keep Atlas's already-shipped chrome — rounded free-edge corners (`radius-lg`) + `shadow-xl` — rather than the reference's flat/no-shadow. Figma: new page + component set `Sheet` (`583:2861`), positioned after Drawer (`577:24`) in the page list. Anatomy mirrors Drawer's Figma mock exactly (header with inline title + close, description, content placeholder, footer placeholder, all on the same token bindings — `surface-overlay` fill, `border`/`border-width/1` stroke, `shadow/xl` effect style, `spacing/6` padding, `spacing/4` gap, `radius/md` placeholder corners); `Side=bottom` alone gets a `border-strong`-filled, `radius/full` 36×4 drag handle (Atlas's own feature, not in the reference — matches Drawer's precedent of no handle on start/end). Code: `compositions/Sheet/Sheet.tsx` re-exports `Dialog as Sheet`, `DialogTrigger`, `DialogHeader`, `DialogTitle`, `DialogDescription`, `DialogBody`, `DialogFooter`, `DialogClose` directly from Dialog (same Radix a11y wiring, zero duplication); only `SheetContent` is new. `Sheet.module.css` lifts Dialog's shipped `.overlay`/`.content`/`.sheet` rules for the bottom case, and reuses Drawer's already-approved start/end geometry (`border-start/end-*-radius`, `inset-block: 0`, size tokens `--atlas-dialog-sm/md/lg/xl/full`, code-only — no Figma Size, matching Drawer) for the two new edge sides, adding a `top` case as the vertical mirror of `bottom`. Safe-area insets use all four existing `--atlas-safe-*` tokens (top/bottom/inline-start/inline-end) — no new tokens needed anywhere. Bug caught and fixed before commit: an early draft put general padding directly on `.content` per side, which would have double-padded against `DialogHeader`/`Body`/`Footer`'s own `--_pad`-based padding (the same custom property, inherited through the DOM since Sheet reuses those exact Dialog components) — fixed to match the established Dialog/Drawer pattern where `.content` only ever adds safe-area padding, never general padding. `app/page.tsx`'s sheet demo migrated from `<DialogContent variant=\"sheet\">` to `<SheetContent side=\"bottom\">`. Dialog.tsx's `DialogVariant` union and its own `.sheet`/`.drawer` CSS are untouched by this task — that removal is the separate, later A3 task, done only once nothing depends on Dialog's sheet presentation either.",
  "date": "2026-09-27"
},
{
  "id": "DEC-029",
  "topic": "Badge tone fill, secondary variant, and primary variant resolved at the A5 audit",
  "decision": "Badge (primitives) DISC-006/015/016 resolved (user, 2026-09-27), all three surfaced at the A5 audit rather than guessed: (1) Figma's success/warning/danger/info tones were drawn solid-fill (tone color + white text) while code used pastel `-subtle` fill (matching Alert's established style) — not caught by the sync's name-only diff. User chose to fix Figma to pastel rather than fix code to solid or add a third solid|subtle|outline appearance axis, since Alert already established `-subtle`/pastel as the system's status-color language. (2) Code's `secondary` variant (bg-subtle grey) had no Figma tone equivalent among the 6 — user chose to drop it from code rather than add a 7th tone to Figma; Figma's `neutral` already matched code's old `default` exactly. (3) Figma's `primary` (solid blue, `--atlas-primary`/`-foreground`) had no code equivalent — user chose to add it as a new code variant rather than defer. Figma: `Appearance` = `default|outline` axis added, crossed with all 6 tones × 3 sizes × 2 states (36→72 variants, node `123:24`); the 4 tone default variants' fills/text rebound from solid `{tone}`/`{tone}-foreground` to `{tone}-subtle`/`{tone}` (base color, not foreground — matches Alert's `color: var(--atlas-{tone})` pattern, also fixing an unrelated white-on-near-white contrast bug in the same lines). New outline variants: transparent fill, stroke bound to `border-width/1`, border+text bound to the tone's border color (neutral→`border-strong`, others→their base tone). Code: `BadgeVariant` = `neutral | primary | success | warning | danger | info` (renamed default→neutral, dropped secondary, dropped outline-as-value); new `BadgeAppearance = \"default\" | \"outline\"` prop; `BadgeIntent` prop removed (redundant once appearance is crossed with variant — tone alone now determines outline color).",
  "date": "2026-09-27"
},
{
